From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] local: drm/msm/dp: drive only the first segment from the PHY behind an LTTPR

With a non-transparent LTTPR the link is trained segment by segment: first
source PHY -> LTTPR, then LTTPR -> sink. Only the first segment is driven by
our PHY. The later ones are driven by the LTTPR, which applies the levels
the source writes to the downstream receiver's TRAINING_LANEx_SET.

msm_dp_ctrl_update_phy_vx_px() calls phy_configure() for every segment. The
last segment trained is the sink's, so its CR phase first resets our PHY to
swing 0 / pre-emphasis 0, and it ends with our PHY at whatever levels the sink
asked the LTTPR for. The first segment, trained moments before to the levels
the LTTPR asked for, is left under- or over-driven.

Seen on the Yoga Slim 7x (PS8830 behind every USB-C port) with a Samsung
C49G95T at 5120x1440@120, HBR3 x4. The sink counts symbol errors every second
on all four lanes. The screen jumps sideways for a frame several times a
minute, and the link occasionally loses lock entirely. The same dock, KVM and
cables are clean from other laptops. dp_debug reports v_level 1 / p_level 0,
which is the sink's adjust request (0x206 = 0x11), not the LTTPR's.

Program the PHY only for the segment directly downstream of it, as i915
does in intel_dp_set_signal_levels() via
intel_dp_phy_is_downstream_of_source(). TRAINING_LANEx_SET is still written
for every segment. link->phy_params, and so dp_debug, still end up holding
the last segment's levels.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -1393,11 +1393,20 @@
 	drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
 		"voltage level: %d emphasis level: %d\n",
 			voltage_swing_level, pre_emphasis_level);
-	ret = msm_dp_ctrl_set_vx_px(ctrl,
-		voltage_swing_level, pre_emphasis_level);
 
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * Behind a non-transparent LTTPR only the first segment is driven by
+	 * this PHY; later segments are driven by the LTTPR from the
+	 * TRAINING_LANEx_SET written below. Reprogramming the PHY there would
+	 * leave the first segment at the last segment's levels.
+	 */
+	if (ctrl->link->lttpr_count <= 0 ||
+	    dp_phy == DP_PHY_LTTPR(ctrl->link->lttpr_count - 1)) {
+		ret = msm_dp_ctrl_set_vx_px(ctrl,
+			voltage_swing_level, pre_emphasis_level);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	if (voltage_swing_level >= DP_TRAIN_LEVEL_MAX) {
 		drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
